# forge-connectivity.rc — Pie half of the MTK CONSYS Wi-Fi userspace for the
# m2note copy of the m5c (LOS 16) file, peripherals lane 2026-09-03.  Vendor rc: parsed inside
# mount_all, i.e. AFTER the ramdisk init.mt6735.rc (the 14.1 rc set carried
# over as the porting base).
#
# The combo-chip side is unchanged and already lives in init.mt6735.rc:
# wmtLoader (/vendor/bin/wmt_loader, class core) probes the chip, conn_launcher
# (/vendor/bin/6620_launcher -p /system/etc/firmware/) stays resident feeding
# WMT_SOC.cfg + WIFI_RAM_CODE_6735; the kernel driver is built in
# (CONFIG_MTK_COMBO_WIFI=y, pie-config) and is powered on/off through
# /dev/wmtWifi.  What Pie changes is who drives that node and who owns the
# supplicant:
#
#  * android.hardware.wifi@1.0-service (user wifi, groups wifi gps inet
#    net_admin net_raw) writes "1"/"0" into WIFI_DRIVER_STATE_CTRL_PARAM
#    (= /dev/wmtWifi, BoardConfig.mk) itself, from libwifi-hal's
#    wifi_load_driver().  ueventd.mt6735.rc (ramdisk) hands the node to
#    system:system, so the HAL fails before wlan0 ever appears.  Regrouped
#    below, m95 shape (ueventd.mt6797.rc line 73: wifi system).
#
#    MEASURED 2026-09-03 14:12 (M5C_LOS16_PERIPHERALS_MEASURE_20260903.md):
#    a chown in `on post-fs-data` is NOT early-proof, it silently does
#    nothing.  /dev/wmtWifi does not exist at kernel init — the chardev
#    (major 153) is created by mtk_wmt_WIFI_chrdev only when wmt_loader
#    probes the combo chip, dmesg [3.907] "WIFI_init: mtk_wmt_WIFI_chrdev
#    driver(major 153) installed", i.e. AFTER post-fs-data has run.  The
#    node then stayed system:system and the HAL died with
#      Failed to access driver state control param Permission denied, 13
#      -> Failed to load WiFi driver -> HalDevMgr: Cannot start IWifi: 9
#      -> WifiNative: Failed to start Hal -> WifiClientModeManager idle.
#    The HAL runs as uid wifi with supplementary groups gps inet net_raw
#    net_admin only (no `system`, read from /proc/<pid>/status), so group
#    rw on a system:system node does not help it either.  Hence the second,
#    late trigger below: wmtLoader is oneshot, so init.svc.wmtLoader=stopped
#    fires exactly once, right after the chardev exists.  The same chown done
#    by hand at that moment produced wlan0 and a 16-network scan on the spot.
#
#  * wpa_supplicant is a HIDL service on Pie (/vendor/bin/hw, sockets under
#    /data/vendor/wifi/wpa) and this tree's external/wpa_supplicant_8 ships no
#    .rc for it (see device/meizu/m95/rootdir/init.m95.connectivity.rc for
#    how that was found the hard way).  The ramdisk init.mt6735.rc still
#    declares the Nougat form (/system/bin/wpa_supplicant -Dnl80211 -c/data/
#    misc/wifi/...), a binary that does not exist on this image; init keeps
#    the FIRST definition of a name and drops later ones ("ignored duplicate
#    definition of service"), hence `override` — a Pie init keyword, verified
#    in system/core/init/service.cpp of this tree.

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/vendor/wifi 0770 wifi wifi
    mkdir /data/vendor/wifi/wpa 0770 wifi wifi
    mkdir /data/vendor/wifi/wpa/sockets 0770 wifi wifi

# The node only exists once wmt_loader (oneshot) has probed the chip.
on property:init.svc.wmtLoader=stopped
    chown wifi system /dev/wmtWifi
    chmod 0660 /dev/wmtWifi

service wpa_supplicant /vendor/bin/hw/wpa_supplicant \
    -O/data/vendor/wifi/wpa/sockets -puse_p2p_group_interface=1 \
    -g@android:wpa_wlan0
    interface android.hardware.wifi.supplicant@1.0::ISupplicant default
    interface android.hardware.wifi.supplicant@1.1::ISupplicant default
    override
    class main
    socket wpa_wlan0 dgram 660 wifi wifi
    group system wifi inet
    disabled
    oneshot
